# Commits

Commits use `type(scope): description` with a coherent scope
(`backend`, `frontend`, `infra`, etc.), without agent `Co-Authored-By`
trailers. Stage explicit paths.

- Format: `type(scope): description` (Conventional Commits).
- Pick one coherent scope for the change, for example `backend`, `frontend`, or `infra`.
- Do not add agent `Co-Authored-By` or `Co-authored-by` trailers.
- Stage explicit paths only. Do not use `git add .` or `git add -A`.

```text
feat(backend): add unlock command queue
fix(frontend): reconnect EventSource after drop
chore(infra): pin MQTT broker version
```
